The 1–5 grade is an evidence and engineering-quality grade, not a measure of a person's intelligence, worth, legal status, or ownership. Grades are provisional until source-level review is completed.

| Area | Present evidence reviewed | Provisional grade | Control / authorship note |
|---|---|---:|---|
| `drivers/` | Kernel driver corpus and Linux licensing/documentation model | 4 | Mature upstream reuse surface; MEARVK controls integration, not historical authorship. |
| `drivers/base/` | Driver-core Kconfig and subsystem structure | 4 | Strong architectural coherence; retain upstream attribution and SPDX. |
| `drivers/acpi/` | Subsystem location and kernel integration role | 3 | Sound upstream subsystem; detailed file-by-file provenance review remains. |
| `drivers/accessibility/` | Subsystem location and kernel integration role | 3 | Sound upstream reuse; README/provenance expansion required. |
| `drivers/amba/` | Subsystem location and kernel integration role | 3 | Clear bus-layer role; source-level authorship inventory remains. |
| `drivers/android/` | Subsystem location and kernel integration role | 3 | Clear platform role; detailed provenance review remains. |
| `drivers/ata/` | Subsystem location and storage role | 3 | Mature subsystem; file-level authorship and modification audit remains. |
| `drivers/atm/` | Subsystem location and networking role | 3 | Legacy subsystem; provenance and maintenance status should be reviewed carefully. |
| `drivers/auxdisplay/` | Subsystem location and display-device role | 3 | Clear role; detailed file-level inventory remains. |
