**Interpretation:** these grades are not claims that every file in an area has the same authorship quality. They are control-surface grades for the current documentation/provenance review. A file-level grade supersedes the directory-level provisional grade when established.

## Authorship reference

**Max Rupplin — MEARVK LLC — 2026** is the current project developer/maintenance reference for Ubuntu Determinant. This reference records project responsibility and genuine modifications; it does not erase upstream authorship, copyright, or licensing.

## Operator attention

Level 4 architectural operators may inspect and modify components within their authorized scope. Their authority creates a duty to preserve provenance, license compliance, security boundaries, reproducibility, and integration evidence.

## Change evidence

A significant property or security change should be traceable through:

```text
source -> change -> commit -> build -> test -> artifact -> integration
```

## Current declaration

As of 2026, Max Rupplin / MEARVK LLC records project-level architectural, maintenance, and integration attention for Ubuntu Determinant. This declaration is subordinate to applicable third-party licenses and existing authorship records.

## Completion objective

The four registers are intended to evolve into a machine-checkable property/concord inventory rather than remain merely narrative documentation.

The driver documentation should ultimately provide one `README.md` per driver directory and subdirectory, generated or maintained from the actual tree so that documentation presence itself is auditable.